      "stageRecord": "The host is an IP with John in Spec-IP, past tense in I, and an intransitive VP headed by leave. This uses the classical GB external-subject configuration rather than a VP-internal subject derivation. Leave assigns its sole participant theta-role to John, and finite I licenses John's nominative Case. The prospective tag is a separate CP with an interrogative C and an IP containing he, past tense, and NegP. Its initially unelided VP also contains leave: this supplies the predicate that will subsequently undergo VP ellipsis. The tag predicate assigns its participant theta-role to he, and tag I licenses nominative Case. Neg takes scope over the tag VP, not over the host. The negative head is represented by the clitic allomorph n't, whose attachment and association with the input token didn't have not yet been established. Both past-tense heads are initially abstract; the host's irregular past realization and the tag's auxiliary support are established in the next stage. No subject movement is required in this version of GB.",
