      "stageRecord": "The complex finite I established in the preceding stage moves to interrogative C, leaving an I trace. Because n't has already incorporated, did and n't move together; the tag subject remains in Spec-IP and follows the auxiliary. This local I-to-C movement satisfies the interrogative head requirement without moving the host verb or either subject. The tag CP is then right-adjoined to the host IP, yielding a recursive IP configuration. This treats the tag as a supplemental clause, not as an argument selected by leave or as coordination with an unpronounced conjunction. The attached clause is licensed as a reversed-polarity tag: the affirmative host supplies the proposition, and the negative tag queries its confirmation. He is referentially identified with John and matches the host subject in third-person singular reference. This is anaphoric coreference rather than syntactic binding: John inside the host IP does not c-command into the adjoined CP. He has no local c-commanding coindexed antecedent in its own finite clause, satisfying Binding Principle B; John likewise has no c-commanding coindexed binder, satisfying Principle C. The full tag VP is retained at this stage so its subsequent ellipsis has an explicit syntactic source.",
